WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.990
If you clicked on this video, then let's just
get this out of the way up front: there are

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.280
major spoilers ahead for the most recent episode
of Game of Thrones.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.909
Last warning before things turn into a spoiler-filled
free-for-all.

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:16.710
Entitled "The Bells," the latest Game of Thrones
episode saw Daenerys Targaryen and her allied

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.370
forces carry out their siege of King's Landing.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:24.730
It all came off the back of Dany witnessing
Cersei Lannister executing her friend Missandei,

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.350
and Daenerys herself executing Varys after
he betrayed her.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.381
Clearly, Daenerys wasn't in the calmest or
most rational state of mind when she and her

00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:35.590
troops rocked up to the Westerosi capital.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.160
Watching Missandei be decapitated, quickly
realizing that people in Westeros love Jon

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.340
Snow and will support his legitimate claim
to the Iron Throne, and understanding that

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.730
she only knows fear in the country proved
too much for Daenerys.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.620
She unleashed fire and fury on King's Landing,
commanding her dragon to burn the city down

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.129
even after its people rang the bells and surrendered.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.120
But it wasn't just dragon fire that blazed
through King's Landing.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.420
Bursts of emerald flames erupted throughout
the city, too.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.440
For those who may not recall, that's Wildfire,
a highly flammable and incredibly volatile

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.190
liquid created by the pyromancers of the ancient
society known as the Alchemists' Guild.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:18.010
Wildfire begins as a bright green liquid and
burns with great strength when it's ignited.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.720
It doesn't carry quite the same properties
as normal fire, as it cannot be extinguished

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.090
with water, only with sand.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.430
Season 8, episode 5 wasn't the first time
viewers caught a glimpse of Wildfire, of course.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:33.080
Cersei utilizes a huge cache of Wildfire hidden
beneath the Sept of Baelor to blow up the

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.440
place of worship during season 6, which kills
then-Queen Margaery Tyrell.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.800
That allows Cersei to claim the Iron Throne
after her son, King Tommen Baratheon takes

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.110
his own life following the fiery carnage.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.890
Wildfire appears in season 2 as well, when
Tyrion Lannister learns that Cersei is planning

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:03.890
to use Wildfire as a weapon of defense against
Stannis Baratheon and his fleet on Blackwater

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.890
Bay.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.530
Tyrion and Bronn pay a visit to the Head of
the Alchemists' Guild in King's Landing, just

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.500
ahead of the Battle of the Blackwater.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.890
The alchemist tells Tyrion and Bronn that
Wildfire might be potent enough to burn off

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.660
people's appendages and then highlights an
intense connection between Wildfire and House

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.690
Targaryen.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:27.310
"After the dragons died, Wildfire was the
key to the Targaryen power."

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.230
Wildfire was discussed again during season
3.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.780
On the fifth episode of that season, Jaime
Lannister reveals the true reason he slaughtered

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:40.920
the Mad King Aerys: the tyrant wanted to burn
every last inch of King's Landing using Wildfire.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.510
The Mad King, realizing that his opponents
were going to win the battle, had his pyromancers

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.450
tuck stores of Wildfire in various locations
throughout King's Landing.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.780
Jaime explains to Brienne of Tarth that the
Mad King was obsessed with the stuff, and

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.620
he loved watching his enemies burn.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:02.430
"He burnt lords he didn't like, he burnt Hands
who disobeyed him, he burnt anyone who was

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.770
against him."

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:09.561
As past seasons have established, Wildfire
is a chosen weapon of House Targaryen, one

00:03:09.561 --> 00:03:14.500
that its members favored when its greatest
advantage over the Seven Kingdoms, their dragons,

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.500
all died out.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.360
It only makes sense that Wildfire would appear
again when Daenerys, the last living child

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.319
of the Mad King, let the devastation of death,
the reality of fear, and the overwhelming

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:28.770
desire for power turn her into a version of
her father.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:33.420
The Mad King attempted to burn King's Landing
with Wildfire and couldn't, but his daughter

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.680
finished the job decades later.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.540
It's almost guaranteed that the Wildfire seen
on season 8, episode 5 came from the stores

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.770
that the Mad King's pyromancers placed across
King's Landing, ones no one had found until

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:48.780
Dany ordered Drogon to blast his flames everywhere.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.959
It also draws yet another terrifying parallel
between Daenerys and her father, the man she

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:57.510
tried so hard not to become up to this point.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.270
Will she suffer the same fate he did, killed
by a knight with a swift hand?

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.569
The final episode of Game of Thrones will
reveal the answer.

